  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Show that $2x^2-x+4>0$ for all $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2\\left(x-\\frac14\\right)^2+\\frac{31}{8}\\ge\\frac{31}{8}>0$ for every real $x$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2-x+4&=2\\left(x^2-\\frac12x\\right)+4\\\\2\\left(x^2-\\frac12x\\right)+4&=2\\left[\\left(x-\\frac14\\right)^2-\\frac1{16}\\right]+4\\\\2\\left[\\left(x-\\frac14\\right)^2-\\frac1{16}\\right]+4&=2\\left(x-\\frac14\\right)^2+\\frac{31}{8}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe squared term is nonnegative for every real $x$. Therefore $2x^2-x+4\\ge\\frac{31}{8}>0$ for every real $x$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
